From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:22:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): synchronize reading space, pager chrome and fast
 scrollbars

Shared with Mihon 0094. Protect leading reading content with the same chrome progress without consuming nested scroll/fling or resizing lazy viewports; keep edge spacers and trailing reachability. Coordinate chrome with visible pager page weights, preserve cancelled swipes, and remove category-settle resets. Follow live track bounds in the current frame, store thumb progress in normalized coordinates, freeze only held finger conversion, and ease only appended-content corrections. Use pixel-based timeline progress. Hide short detail chapter scrollbars using runtime viewport/column density, retaining long-list dragging. Connect passive browse lists and missing source panorama entry points to the shared fast scroller. Use 36dp compact primary/secondary rows, with at most 2dp status trimming clamped to camera cutout; preserve normal/large-font sizes and transparent details. Add held pager, content geometry, append correction, grab travel and short-detail regressions; update existing compact header tests.
